The following is a timeline of the  [LINK: (Sudanese civil war (2023–present)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudanese_civil_war_(2023%E2%80%93present)]  in 2026.

This timeline is a dynamic and fluid list, and as such may never satisfy criteria of completeness. Moreover, some events may only be fully understood and/or discovered in retrospect.


# JANUARY #

Hamid Ali Abubakar, the commander-in-chief of the  [LINK: (RSF) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rapid_Support_Forces] -aligned faction of the  [LINK: (Sudanese Awakening Revolutionary Council) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudanese_Awakening_Revolutionary_Council]  (RAC) and concurrent security adviser to  [LINK: (Hemedti) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hemedti] , was killed in a drone strike on a meeting of RSF and allied commanders in Damrat al-Firdous,  [LINK: (Central Darfur) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Darfur] . [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-1]

The RSF carried out drone strikes on  [LINK: (El-Obeid) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/El-Obeid]  and  [LINK: (White Nile State) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_Nile_State] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-2]  An airstrike against a power station in El-Obeid left the city without electricity. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-3]  [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-4]

Up to 64 civilians were killed in  [LINK: (SAF) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudanese_Armed_Forces]  airstrikes on Hemedti's hometown of  [LINK: (Al Zorg) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al_Zorg]  that destroyed the town's hospital, and also killed two of Hemedti's relatives and local tribal leader Bashir Barma Baraka Allah. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-5]

The RSF and allied groups claimed to have taken El Bardab, north of  [LINK: (Kadugli) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kadugli] . [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-6]

The  [LINK: (Sudan Liberation Movement-Abdel Wahid) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudan_Liberation_Movement/Army]  (SLM-AW), a neutral rebel group, ordered the replacement of Sudanese state symbols with its own in the  [LINK: (Liberated Areas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liberated_Areas]  in Central and  [LINK: (North Darfur) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Darfur] . [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-7]

The SAF claimed to have intercepted a drone attack by the RSF on  [LINK: (Merowe) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merowe,_Sudan] . [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-8]

Thirteen people, including eight children, were killed in an RSF drone strike on a house in El-Obeid, according to the Sudan Doctors' Network. [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-9]

One soldier was killed in a suspected RSF drone strike on a  [LINK: (Sudan Shield Forces) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudan_Shield_Forces]  camp in the  [LINK: (Butana) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butana]  plains in  [LINK: (Gezira State) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gezira_State] . [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-10]

The RSF and its allies, the  [LINK: (Sudan Liberation Forces Gathering) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudan_Liberation_Movement/Army#Sudan_Liberation_Forces_Alliance]  and the  [LINK: (Justice and Equality Movement) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Justice_and_Equality_Movement] , attacked positions of the  [LINK: (Darfur Joint Protection Force) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darfur_Joint_Protection_Force]  (JDF) at the  [LINK: (Chad–Sudan border) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chad%E2%80%93Sudan_border] . [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-11]

The SAF carried out airstrikes on RSF positions in  [LINK: (Darfur) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darfur]  and  [LINK: (Kordofan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kordofan] . The army claimed 240 military vehicles were wrecked and hundreds of RSF members were killed. The army also claimed a Turkish  [LINK: (Baykar Bayraktar Akıncı) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baykar_Bayraktar_Ak%C4%B1nc%C4%B1]  drone operated by the RSF was shot down over  [LINK: (Nyala Airport) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyala_Airport] . In  [LINK: (South Kordofan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Kordofan] , the  [LINK: (SPLM-N (al-Hilu)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudan_People%27s_Liberation_Movement%E2%80%93North]  said 13 civilians, including children, were killed in an airstrike on Um Jamina in Al-Sunut County. [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-12]

The JDF accused the RSF of killing and kidnapping 19 people in Jirjira, North Darfur. [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-13]

The SAF conducted strikes against a supply convoy in  [LINK: (Yabus) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yabus] ,  [LINK: (Blue Nile State) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Nile_State] , near the  [LINK: (Ethiopia–Sudan border) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethiopia%E2%80%93Sudan_border] . [LINK: ([14]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-14]

The SAF-aligned government announced its complete return to  [LINK: (Khartoum) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khartoum] , having operated in  [LINK: (Port Sudan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_Sudan]  as the temporary capital since 2022. [LINK: ([15]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-15]

Five people were killed and 20 injured in an RSF drone strike on a market in Kartala,  [LINK: (South Kordofan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Kordofan] . [LINK: ([16]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-16]

At least 27 people were killed and 73 others were wounded by an RSF drone strike on an army base in  [LINK: (Singa) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singa,_Sudan] . The attack reportedly targeted a meeting between government and SAF officials at the base. The governors of White Nile,  [LINK: (Sennar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sennar_State] , and Blue Nile States were confirmed to have been in attendance, but survived the attack. [LINK: ([17]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-17]  [LINK: ([18]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-18]

The SAF and allied groups claimed to have retaken Jirjira from the RSF. [LINK: ([19]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-19]

The SAF repelled an attack by the RSF and SPLM-N (al-Hilu) near Al-Kuwaik, close to  [LINK: (Kadugli) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kadugli] . [LINK: ([20]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-20]

The RSF was accused of abducting 97 young men from a gold mine in Eyal Bakhit,  [LINK: (West Kordofan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Kordofan] . [LINK: ([21]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-21]

The RSF carried out a cross-border attack into Chad while pursuing a JDF unit that fled into the country, killing seven Chadian soldiers at the Birak garrison near  [LINK: (Tiné Djagaraba) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tin%C3%A9_Djagaraba] . [LINK: ([22]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-22]  [LINK: ([23]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-23]

Twelve people were killed in an RSF drone strike on a market in  [LINK: (Dalang, South Kordofan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dalang,_South_Kordofan] . [LINK: ([24]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-24]

The SPLM-N (al-Hilu) and the RSF claimed to have repelled an SAF attack on Habila, 30 km (19 mi) from Dalang. [LINK: ([25]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-25]

The SAF repelled a large scale RSF attack on Wadi al-Hout in  [LINK: (North Kordofan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_Kordofan] . [LINK: ([26]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-26]

The  [LINK: (Central Bank of Sudan) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Bank_of_Sudan]  announced the resumption of its operations in Khartoum for the first time since the civil war began. [LINK: ([27]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-27]

The RSF detained 17  [LINK: (Zaghawas) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zaghawa_people]  from Mahajeriya in  [LINK: (East Darfur) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Darfur] , including the head of the rural court. [LINK: ([28]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-28]

Five people were killed in an SAF drone strike on a market in Abu Zaima, North Kordofan. [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-zaima-29]

Two people were killed in an RSF drone strike on Dalang. [LINK: ([30]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-30]  The RSF claimed to have shot down an SAF  [LINK: (Bayraktar) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baykar_Bayraktar_family]  drone over the city. [LINK: ([29]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-zaima-29]

The SAF repelled a large-scale attack by the RSF and SPLM-N (al-Hilu) from South Sudan on Milkan and Al-Silak in  [LINK: (Blue Nile State) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Nile_State] . [LINK: ([31]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-31]

The SAF retook Habila and broke the  [LINK: (siege) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Dilling]  of  [LINK: (Dalang) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dalang,_South_Kordofan] . [LINK: ([32]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-32]

Five people were killed in a drone strike on Dalang. [LINK: ([33]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-33]

Dozens of people were killed in an RSF drone strike on Dalang. [LINK: ([34]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-34]

The European Union imposed sanctions on seven individuals for their role in escalating the conflict in Sudan, including Hemedti's brother Major Algoney Hamdan Dagalo Musa and Al-Misbah Abu Zaid Talha, commander of the SAF-allied  [LINK: (Al-Bara' ibn Malik Battalion) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Bara%27_ibn_Malik_Battalion] . [LINK: ([35]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_the_Sudanese_civil_war_(2026)#cite_note-35]


